  "title": "Sony brings AI upscaling to the regular PS5",
  "narration": "Sony just brought AI upscaling to the regular PS5. Until now, PlayStation Spectral Super Resolution was a PS5 Pro feature because it was too computationally expensive. The new version is called QSSR: a smaller neural network, hand-tuned to run on base PS5 hardware. Sony says it improves detail and image stability, with Marvel’s Wolverine and Ghost of Yōtei getting support first. But PSSR on PS5 Pro is still the higher-quality option. So your five-year-old console just got a little Pro-ish, without actually becoming a Pro.",
